{#
  The portal's notice area: one fixed container in the top-right corner of the
  viewport holding the toasts.

  Two things fill it. The server's `flash` messages — one-shot, queued by the
  previous request, and emptied as they are read, so a reload never shows the
  same message twice — are rendered here. Anything a page bundle has to say
  after a fetch is appended to the same container by `window.CRM.portalToast()`.

  The container is `position: fixed`, so a notice never takes part in the
  document flow and nothing on the page moves when one appears.

  A THEME THAT OVERRIDES layout.html.twig MUST KEEP THIS INCLUDE. Without it
  there is no container, and every "Your details have been saved." in the portal
  goes unseen.
#}
<div class="portal-toasts" id="portal-toasts" role="status" aria-live="polite">
    {% for message in flash %}
    {% set type = message.type|default('info') %}
    <div class="portal-flash portal-flash-{{ type }}" role="status">
        <i class="fa-solid {{ {
            'success': 'fa-circle-check',
            'warning': 'fa-triangle-exclamation',
            'danger': 'fa-circle-exclamation'
        }[type]|default('fa-circle-info') }} portal-flash-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="portal-flash-text">{{ message.message }}</span>
        <button class="portal-flash-dismiss" type="button"
                aria-label="{{ gettext('Dismiss') }}">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
</div>
